# React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind

## Stack

- Use **React 18**, **TypeScript**, and **Tailwind CSS**.
- Prefer functional components; do not introduce class components.

## Styling

- Style with Tailwind utility classes first.
- Avoid inline `style={{ ... }}` unless a value cannot be expressed with Tailwind (e.g. dynamic runtime values).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button style={{ padding: '8px 16px', backgroundColor: '#2563eb' }}>Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white">Save</button>
```

## Components + JSDoc

- Export functional components typed with TypeScript.
- Add a JSDoc comment describing the component’s purpose (and notable props when non-obvious).

```tsx
type ButtonProps = {
  label: string;
  onClick: () => void;
};

/**
 * Primary action button.
 * Uses Tailwind classes for layout and color.
 */
export function Button({ label, onClick }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button
      type="button"
      className="rounded bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
      onClick={onClick}
    >
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}
```
